FORMAT: 1A
HOST: https://sandbox-partner-api.orangehealth.dev/

# Partner API Public Order Flow
#### Base URL :

- Testing : `https://sandbox-partner-api.orangehealth.dev`
- Production : `https://partner-api.orangehealth.in`
    

#### Business Logic :

Please reach out to [integrations@orangehealth.in](https://mailto:integrations@orangehealth.in) in order to get your personalised api key for testing, we will create a partner entity that best suits your business needs and share the api key through mail for testing.

Based on the payment collection needs we broadly classify partners as :

- Payment always collected by partner (You collect the payment for each order from the patient and settle with OrangeHealth on a monthly or weekly basis)
- Payment always collected by OrangeHealth (We collect the payment for each order from the patient and credit your earnings)
- Payment decided at order level (You can choose which order has to be collected by OrangeHealth and which ones will be collected by you)
    

#### Auth:

> Add a header as follows (key, value) :  
(api_key : YOUR_API_KEY_HERE) 
  

If you do not have your own API Key and want to explore our APIs initially we have 3 public API keys based on the 3 broad classifications given above

- Payment always collected by partner : `partner-alwaysPartner`
- Payment always collected by OrangeHealth : `partner-alwaysOH`
- Payment decided at order level : `partner-decidedAtOrderLevel`


## Fetch Serviceability [/v1/partner/serviceability{?latitude,longitude,request_date}]
___
#### Location :

For all testing purposes please fetch latitude and longitude from the geofence shown in this [map](https://www.google.com/maps/d/viewer?mid=1kl_3fWKspPnnZZ_m2jJaguEvENgJTso&usp=sharing).  
For production, we will share the geofence we service through mail

For organisations that do not fetch the accurate lat and long from the customer, we have pincode based serviceability check as well.
However, if pincode is used instead of lat and long, we do not provide slots, request has to be created without the selection of slots and our internal team will reach out to the patient to capture the exact location before confirming the slots.

Note: Latitude-longitude gives the available slots and pincode say whether the location is serviceable or not

### Fetch Serviceability [GET]
+ Parameters
  + latitude (number, optional) - Latitude of the sample pick up location. 13.0240 for testing on sandbox
  + longitude (number, optional) - Longitude of the sample pick up location. 77.6433 for testing on sandbox
  + request_date (string, required) - Date of sample pick up in YYYY-MM-DD format. Date has to be >= today (mandatory)
  + pincode (string, optional) - Pincode of the location, in case lat and long is not available. 560043 for testing on sandbox
  
  
+ Request
    + Header
        ```
        api_key:<value>
        ```

+ Response 200 (application/json)

    + Attributes
        + description: Example response where the location is serviceable and the slots are available.
        + response body (object)
            + status: Tells if the location is serviceable or not
            + slots (object)
                + YYYY-MM-DDThh:mm:ss (object)
                    +  slot_datetime: YYYY-MM-DDThh:mm:ss [Same as the key]
                    + is_morning_slot (boolean):
                    + is_afternoon_slot (boolean):
                    + is_evening_slot (boolean):

    + Body
    ```json
    {
    "status": "Location is serviceable",
    "slots": {
        "2023-04-22T07:15:00": {
            "slot_datetime": "2023-04-22T07:15:00",
            "is_morning_slot": true,
            "is_afternoon_slot": false,
            "is_evening_slot": false
        },
        "2023-04-22T08:15:00": {
