}```

+ Response 400 (application/json)
    + Attributes
        + status : invalid request id or token is passed
        Could not get request details, re-verify request ID and token provided

    + Body
    ```json
    {
        "status": "Could not get request details, re-verify request ID and token provided"
    }
    ```
    

  
## Get Test Results [/v1/partner/test-results{?creation_start_date,creation_end_date,request_id,patient_id}]
___

This request returns all the test-level parameters provided the partner is allowed to request them. (Configurable through OH end, please get in touch with [integrations@orangehealth.in](https://mailto:integrations@orangehealth.in) for the same)

Things to note:

1. Three filters can be used:
    1. **Date range filter**
    2. **Request ID**
    3. **Patient ID**
    4. **primary_patient_number**
2. One of the filters is required to query the data.
3. The date range filter requires `creation_start_date` and `creation_end_date` to be provided with a difference of **7 days or less**. The dates should be provided in `YYYY-MM-DD` format and are presumed to be in the **IST timezone.**
4. You can provide more than one request ID
5. You can provide more than one patient ID
6. See all the examples in the collection for all successful responses and all possible error messages.

### Get Test Results [GET]

+ Parameters
  + creation_start_date (required, string) - Order completion start date in the date range filter.
  + creation_end_date (required,string) - Order completion end date in the date range filter.
  + request_id - Request ID provided to partners after an order is placed, more than one can be sent
  + patient_id - Patient ID from Orange health database, more than one can be sent.
  + primary_patient_number - phone number used to create an order, only one can be sent 

+ Request
    + Header
        ```
        api_key:<value>
        ```
    
+ Response 200 (application/json)

    + Body
    ```json
