### task.confirmed explanation [POST]

If the request payload in Create Order API has the correct lat and long, our system will automatically confirm the collection and task.confirmed will be triggered for each patient as follows.
If the lat and long is missing, our team will get in touch with the end customer to fetch the right location, after which the task.confirmed event will be triggered for each patient.


### task.confirmed (Jane Doe) [POST]

+ Request
    + Header
        ```
        x-oh-signature:1b34af6a24e72b2bc871890c39b4f2f6efc9ca6ed1dcb2ff410ec575a60e4c4f
        x-oh-event-id:362c9911-cae0-424a-a55a-23997960d127
        ```
    
+ Response 200 (application/json)

    + Body
```json
{
  "event": "task.confirmed",
  "contains": [
    "request",
    "invoice",
    "customer_details",
    "payment_details",
    "tasks",
    "order",
    "city_code",
    "reports"
  ],
  "payload": {
    "customer_details": {
      "created_on": "2022-02-16 06:52:52",
      "id": 60936,
      "name": "John Doe",
      "number": "9999999999",
      "system_customer_id": 3517,
      "system_customer_user_id": 5897
    },
    "invoice": {
      "city_request_id": "BLR0",
