### order.completed explanation [POST]
As and when all the tests within a particular order (at patient level) is completed, order.completed will be triggered

Suppose patient X has 2 tests under 1 order,
The events triggered would be 
- test.completed_sent (1/2 test completed)
- test.completed_sent (2/2 test completed)
- order.completed (1/1 order completed due to 2/2 tests completed)

Reports for the entire order merged can be found in this event

This will also be the terminal state of the respective order since it is completed

